e security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"November–April (dry, whale-watching, winter N-swell surf)","shoulder":"May–June & October","green":"July–September into early October (hot, hurricane/chubasco, summer S-swell)","booking_lead":"3–5+ months for peak boutique inventory (small supply)","off_season_specials":"Green-season summer surf + desert-wellness value; disclose storm risk + insurance","event_peaks":"Christmas/New Year, Semana Santa, whale Jan–Mar, surf winter N-swell Nov–Mar + summer S-swell Jun–Sep","campaign_start":"Late summer/early fall for Nov–Apr peak; late spring for green-season surf/wellness"},"jewels":[{"name":"Gallery walk + Hotel California","si_tag":"Culture & Arts","status":"future","hook":"Pueblo Mágico galleries + the mythic Hotel California","bookable_category":"free stroll / dining","tier":"essential","source":"https://incabotravel.com/uncover-todos-santos-hotel-california-myths-facts-must-visit-spots (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"Culture & Arts","blurb":"Pueblo Mágico galleries + the mythic Hotel California","when":"year-round","commission":"adjacent dining/hotel package","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Offshore whale-watching (Punta Lobos)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Gray + humpback panga tours, fewer crowds than Cabo","bookable_category":"panga tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://omegatours.mx/whale-watching/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"expedition","blurb":"Gray + humpback panga tours, fewer crowds than Cabo","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Magdalena Bay whale extension","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Gray-whale nursery close encounters (Jan–Mar)","bookable_category":"guided day/overnight extension","tier":"premier","source":"https://serendipityventures.com/whale-watching/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"expedition","blurb":"Gray-whale nursery close encounters (Jan–Mar)","commission":"DMC / activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Playa Los Cerritos surf + safe swim","si_tag":"Surf / Ocean Adventures","status":"future","hook":"Best all-round break AND the area''s gentlest swim beach","bookable_category":"surf school / rental","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.amyrextodossantos.com/amy-rex-in-todos-santos/navigating-the-beautiful-beaches-of-todos-santoscerritos-area-safety-tips-for-visitors (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"Surf / Ocean Adventures","blurb":"Best all-round break AND the area''s gentlest swim beach","commission":"activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Playa San Pedrito advanced surf","si_tag":"Surf / Ocean Adventures","status":"future","hook":"Powerful break for experienced surfers (no swimming)","bookable_category":"guided surf","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g1636027-d10954417-Reviews-Playa_San_Pedrito-El_Pescadero_Baja_California.html (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"Surf / Ocean Adventures","blurb":"Powerful break for experienced surfers (no swimming)","commission":"activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Desert-wellness retreat (Paradero-class)","si_tag":"Wellness & Spa","status":"future","hook":"Sierra-La-Laguna desert wellness immersion","bookable_category":"resort / host-Virtuoso","tier":"luxury","source":"https://cabovisitor.com/where-to-stay-in-todos-santos/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"November–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wellness","blurb":"Sierra-La-Laguna desert wellness immersion","when":"November–April","commission":"on application / host program","accessed":"2026-07-04"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is Todos Santos known for?","a":"It''s a designated Pueblo Mágico — Baja''s Pacific art town of galleries, mango orchards and the mythic Hotel California (the Eagles'' band denies a direct link), an hour and a world away from the Los Cabos corridor. Come for galleries, sunsets and surf, not a swim resort.","source":"loscabosguide.com / incabotravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"When can I see whales from Todos Santos?","a":"Late December through April, best January–March, when gray and humpback whales pass the Pacific coast on Punta Lobos panga tours; multi-hour or overnight Magdalena Bay extensions reach the gray-whale nursery for close, calf encounters.","source":"todossantosvillarentals.com / serendipityventures.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the real danger here?","a":"The Pacific surf, not crime. Most Todos Santos beaches have strong rip currents and backwash that have caused drownings — do not swim them; stick to the Cerritos protected zone and defer to on-the-ground flags. Hurricane season runs Jun–Nov.","source":"amyrextodossantos.com / mexiconewsdaily.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Todos Santos Travel Guide — Pueblo Mágico Art Town, Surf & Whales | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Baja''s Pacific art town: Hotel California, gallery walks, Cerritos surf, offshore whale-watching, and straight beach-safety guidance (most beaches are riptide-dangerous).","slug":"todos-santos-mexico","primary_keyword":"Todos Santos Mexico travel guide","long_tail":["Todos Santos beaches safe to swim","Cerritos vs San Pedrito surf","Hotel California Todos Santos","whale watching Todos Santos","best boutique hotels Todos Santos"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Todos Santos Pueblo Mágico","playas de Todos Santos se puede nadar","Hotel California Todos Santos","surf Playa Cerritos San Pedrito","avistamiento de ballenas Todos Santos","hoteles boutique Todos Santos"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"wellness","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Hotel San Cristóbal (Bunkhouse by Hyatt) / San Cristóbal Baja","why_ultra":"Pacific-overlooking boutique, 32 rooms, MICHELIN Key, chapel + restaurant; premier–luxury boutique (not branded-ultra)","earning":"on application / via host program (Hyatt/Bunkhouse)","virtuoso_value_add":"verify","mor":true},{"name":"Paradero Todos Santos","why_ultra":"Wellness resort on ~5 desert acres, 41 large suites, virgin Pacific beaches + Sierra La Laguna; luxury boutique","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso (verify)","virtuoso_value_add":"verify","mor":true},{"name":"Guaycura Boutique Hotel, Beach Club & Spa","why_ultra":"19th-c. town-center building, rooftop infinity pool, El Faro Beach Club & Spa; premier boutique","earning":"on application / via host program","virtuoso_value_add":"verify","mor":true}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Todos Santos, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":23.4469,"lng":-110.2247}}'::jsonb, 112),
  ('torres-del-paine-chile', '10S', 'Torres del Paine & Chilean Patagonia', 'Chile', 'Three granite towers and the wind', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Lakes, Patagonia & Easter Island', '{"expedition","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"131","emergency_all":{"ambulance_samu":"131","police_carabineros":"133","fire_bomberos":"132"},"advisory_level":"L2","advisory_source":"travel.state.gov, updated 2026-05-20, accessed 2026-07-07","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","air_access_verified":true,"remote_flag":true,"weather_headline":"Patagonian wind (gusts 100+ km/h), 4-seasons-in-a-day, hypothermia risk, river crossings; guided reduces risk","water":"park streams generally potable — note, not guaranteed","evac_chain":"Puerto Natales clinic -> Punta Arenas hospital -> Santiago; air-evac available but expensive/slow — travel+medical-evac insurance strongly indicated","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chile","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-08-18T23:18:12+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Feb (austral summer; Jan busiest + windiest)","shoulder":["Oct-Nov","Mar-Apr"],"green_winter":"May-Sep (O-circuit closed; winter puma-tracking; reduced lodge inventory)","booking_window":"W-trek 5-6 months ahead; refugios/EcoCamp/premium lodges 6-12 months ahead; two-operator bed release Apr-Jun","inflection":"season release (Apr-Jun) — peak dates clear within weeks","fire_date":"late-Mar / early-Apr (curve-start minus 1-2 weeks) for Dec-Feb inventory"},"jewels":[{"name":"Base Las Torres at sunrise","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.swoop-patagonia.com/chile/torres-del-paine","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the pre-dawn push to catch the three towers lit alpenglow-red over Lake Torre; the signature image of Patagonia","si":"expedition","blurb":"the pre-dawn push to catch the three towers lit alpenglow-red over Lake Torre; the signature image of Patagonia","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"guided sunrise day-hike (Chile Nativo / EcoCamp / lodge)"},{"name":"French Valley (Valle del Frances)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.swoop-patagonia.com/chile/torres-del-paine","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the middle arm of the W, waterfalls and hanging glaciers under the Cuernos","si":"expedition","blurb":"the middle arm of the W, waterfalls and hanging glaciers under the Cuernos","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"W-trek segment (guided/self-guided)"},{"name":"Grey Glacier (boat / kayak / ice-hike)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://torres-del-paine.org/","hook":"three tiers of intimacy with a calving ice-field arm","si":"expedition","blurb":"three tiers of intimacy with a calving ice-field arm","commission":"outfitter boat + guided kayak/ice-hike"},{"name":"Lago Pehoe + Cuernos / Nordenskjold line","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.swoop-patagonia.com/chile/torres-del-paine","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the classic postcard: the black-capped Cuernos del Paine over impossibly turquoise glacial lakes; the Pehoé viewpoint and lakeshore lodge frame it","si":"expedition","blurb":"the classic postcard: the black-capped Cuernos del Paine over impossibly turquoise glacial lakes; the Pehoé viewpoint and lakeshore lodge frame it","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"scenic day tour / lodge excursion"},{"name":"Winter puma-tracking safari","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"luxury","source":"https://www.ecocamp.travel/blog/torres-del-paine-in-winter","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"May–Sep specialist trackers under windless Antarctic high-pressure skies; the counter-seasonal luxe wildlife product","si":"expedition","blurb":"May–Sep specialist trackers under windless Antarctic high-pressure skies; the counter-seasonal luxe wildlife product","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"guided winter puma program (specialist trackers)"},{"name":"Balmaceda-Serrano fjord (Ultima Esperanza)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.howlanders.com/en/tours-chile/puerto-natales","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"full-day glacier boat from Puerto Natales to the Serrano and Balmaceda glaciers","si":"expedition","blurb":"full-day glacier boat from Puerto Natales to the Serrano and Balmaceda glaciers","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"outfitter day cruise from Puerto Natales"},{"name":"Milodon Cave (Cueva del Milodon)","si_tag":"GEA/Heritage","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.howlanders.com/en/tours-chile/puerto-natales","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA/Heritage","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"half-day tour / park-transfer add-on"},{"name":"Punta Arenas + Magdalena Island penguins","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.howlanders.com/en/tours-chile/punta-arenas/magdalena-island-penguin-tour","hook":"a boat across the Strait of Magellan to a colony of ~thousands of Magellanic penguins","si":"expedition","blurb":"a boat across the Strait of Magellan to a colony of ~thousands of Magellanic penguins","commission":"outfitter half/full-day (Oct-Mar)"},{"name":"Petrohue Waterfalls + Osorno Volcano (Lake District)","si_tag":"GEA/RHN","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.veloso.com/chile/puerto-varas/excursions/osorno-volcano-petrohue-waterfalls/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"The Osorno summit climb and Villarrica ascents require guides, crampons, ice-axe and weather windows; glaciated and crevasse-exposed. Never sold as a walk-up","si":"GEA/RHN","blurb":"The Osorno summit climb and Villarrica ascents require guides, crampons, ice-axe and weather windows; glaciated and crevasse-exposed. Never sold as a walk-up","when":"year-round","commission":"full-day tour / Lake District DMC"},{"name":"Chiloe — palafitos + UNESCO wooden churches (Castro)","si_tag":"GEA/RHN","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.cascada.travel/blog/from-penguins-to-palafitos-everything-you-should-do-on-chiloe","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the largest concentration of stilt houses in Chile and 16 UNESCO-listed timber Jesuit churches; curanto pit-feasts and rare mixed Humboldt/Magellanic penguin colonies at Ancud","si":"GEA/RHN","blurb":"the largest concentration of stilt houses in Chile and 16 UNESCO-listed timber Jesuit churches; curanto pit-feasts and rare mixed Humboldt/Magellanic penguin colonies at Ancud","when":"year-round","commission":"Chiloe DMC extension from Puerto Varas"},{"name":"Easter Island / Rapa Nui (moai) — remote member","si_tag":"romance","tier":"luxury","source":"https://www.micetraveladvisor.com/news/article/easter-island-chile-complete-2026-travel-guide-to-rapa-nuis-moai-sites-flights-from-santiago-and-national-park-rules/","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Folded in as a jewel and flagged remoteflag: true. It shares the subregion string but is a 5.5–6.5-hour flight from the mainland","si":"romance","blurb":"Folded in as a jewel and flagged remoteflag: true. It shares the subregion string but is a 5.5–6.5-hour flight from the mainland","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"LATAM flight affiliate + Rapa Nui guide/lodge package"}],"faq":[{"q":"How far ahead do you need to book the Torres del Paine W-trek?","a":"Book the W-trek about 5–6 months ahead, and refugios, EcoCamp or premium lodges 6–12 months ahead for peak dates. That lead time is forced by the two-operator refugio system — Las Torres Patagonia and Vértice Patagonia release beds in stages (roughly April–June) and peak dates clear within weeks. If a date shows \"sold out,\" monitor for freed beds, as cancellations spike 2–4 weeks pre-travel.","source":"reservenature.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Which lodges make Torres del Paine a honeymoon?","a":"The all-inclusive luxe tier — explora, Tierra Patagonia and Awasi — turns the wilderness into a private-guide couples trip with villas, open bars and hot tubs facing the Cuernos. Awasi is the apex: 14 stand-alone private villas on a private reserve, each with its own dedicated guide and 4x4 for bespoke daily excursions.","source":"awasi.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What does \"all-inclusive\" mean at a Patagonia lodge?","a":"It means one nightly rate bundles lodging, all meals, open bar and daily guided excursions — structurally the same all-inclusive lane TWW tracks in the Caribbean, expressed as wilderness luxe rather than beach resort. explora Patagonia, Tierra Patagonia and Awasi all run this model at the park.","source":"patagonline.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"all_inclusive-model"},{"q":"Can you add Easter Island to a Torres del Paine trip?","a":"Only as its own standalone leg, not a day add-on. Easter Island (Rapa Nui) is a LATAM-monopoly flight of 5.5–6.5 hours from the mainland, with its own FUI entry form, a ~USD 80 park ticket (10-day validity) and a mandatory local guide inside the park. It shares the sub_region string but is 3,700 km out in the Pacific, so price and route it separately.","source":"micetraveladvisor.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Torres del Paine?","a":"The environment, not people. Notorious Patagonian wind — gusts of 100+ km/h — can knock a hiker off a trail, and you should expect four seasons in a day, with hypothermia a live risk even in summer plus river crossings and steep moraine. Wind and whiteout can close Base Torres and French Valley at short notice, so guided trips and buffer days materially reduce risk.","source":"blogpatagonia.australis.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the Grey Glacier ice-hike dangerous?","a":"It runs only as a guided activity, and it is never sold unguided. Walking on the glacier requires crampons, a harness and a certified guide, with an advance reservation required — the crampons, roped travel and guide judgment are the whole safety system on a live, crevassed ice-field arm. The Grey Lake kayak among icebergs is likewise guided-only for the same cold-water and calving hazards.","source":"torres-del-paine.org, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Torres del Paine & Chilean Patagonia — W-Trek, O-Circuit, Lodges & the Lake District | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-CL","local_keywords":["Torres del Paine trekking","circuito W Torres del Paine","circuito O Torres del Paine reservas","qué hacer en Puerto Natales","glaciar Grey kayak","mejor época para visitar Torres del Paine","volcán Osorno Puerto Varas","pingüinos isla Magdalena Punta Arenas"],"hreflang":["en","es-CL"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"explora Patagonia (Salto Chico)","type":"all-inclusive lodge in-park","earning":"luxe hotel-commission band","mor":"where contracted","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Tierra Patagonia","type":"all-inclusive lodge park-edge (Lago Sarmiento)","earning":"luxe hotel-commission band","mor":"where contracted","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Awasi Patagonia","type":"Relais & Chateaux private villas + private guide/4x4","earning":"ultra commission band","mor":"where contracted","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"EcoCamp Patagonia","type":"geodesic-dome glamping in-park","earning":"premium-package commission","mor":"operator/consortium","tier":"premium-luxe"},{"name":"The Singular Patagonia","type":"boutique fjord hotel (Puerto Natales)","earning":"luxe hotel-commission band","mor":"where contracted","tier":"luxe"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Torres del Paine & Chilean Patagonia, Chile"},"geo":{"lat":-50.9423,"lng":-73.4068}}'::jsonb, 113),
  ('tortuguero-costa-rica', '10S', 'Tortuguero', 'Costa Rica', 'Canals and the green turtle nesting coast', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Costa Rica', '{"expedition","river"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Boat-only access — no road reaches the village; arrive via La Pavona/Moín boat or TTQ airstrip + boat transfer","~22,500 green-turtle females nest annually — top green-turtle nesting site in the Western Hemisphere","Green turtle nesting Jul 1–Oct 15 (peak Jul–Aug, hatch Sep–Oct); leatherback Feb–Apr","Freshwater canal network (''Little Amazon''): 442 birds, 138 mammals, 118 reptiles, 58 amphibians","Sea Turtle Conservancy (est. 1959, Dr. Archie Carr) runs the world''s longest continuous sea-turtle research project here"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","nearest_hospital":"Hospital de Guápiles (+506 2710 6801); San José (CIMA / Clínica Bíblica) for major trauma","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_note":"Exercise Increased Caution — crime, rip currents; updated Apr 2, 2026","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":true,"remote_flag":true,"hazards":["boat_safety_canals","guided_only_turtle_tours_no_flash","heat_humidity","caiman_crocodile_no_swimming","rip_currents_beach"],"health":{"malaria":"low/negligible (flag: consult provider; residual Caribbean/Limón zone)","dengue":"primary mosquito risk; wet-season spike May–Nov; use repellent","water":"bottled/filtered in remote lodges"},"fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-19T11:42:25+01:00"}},"timing":{"curve_start":"late June / early July","peak":"Jul-Aug (nesting) into Sep-Oct (hatching + drier micro-season)","seasonality_note":"Inverts national dry-season pattern; driven by green-turtle nesting Jul-Oct; leatherback Feb-Apr; Caribbean coast wettest but Sep-Oct comparatively drier here","booking_lead":"weeks ahead; night tours capped 15/visit, same-day lottery","fire_date":"2026-06-15 to 2026-06-22 (primary); secondary ~mid-August","flag":"biological not event-driven; sharpen on live tracking"},"jewels":[{"name":"Night green-turtle nesting walk (Jul–Oct)","si_tag":"GEA/Wildlife","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.tortugueronationalpark.com/tortuguero-turtle-nesting-season/","hook":"GUIDED-ONLY — certified park guide legally required No white light, no flash photography, red-light only, dark non-reflective clothing, stay behind guide, 15-person cap","si":"GEA/Wildlife","blurb":"GUIDED-ONLY — certified park guide legally required No white light, no flash photography, red-light only, dark non-reflective clothing, stay behind guide, 15-person cap","commission":"lodge-package override + STC conservation add-on"},{"name":"Dawn canal boat safari","si_tag":"GEA/RCR","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.entercostarica.com/attractions/national-parks-and-refuges/tortuguero","timing":"Jul-Aug  into Sep-Oct","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Guided Life vests, licensed/permitted operator, no swimming, no hand-trailing in water","si":"GEA/RCR","blurb":"Guided Life vests, licensed/permitted operator, no swimming, no hand-trailing in water","when":"Jul-Aug  into Sep-Oct","commission":"in-package or standalone boat tour via DMC/lodge"},{"name":"Kayak/canoe the caños (incl. Caño Palma)","si_tag":"RCR/GEA","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.twoweeksincostarica.com/tortuguero-canals-boat-tour/","timing":"Jul-Aug  into Sep-Oct","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Can be unguided but guide advised Caiman & crocodile awareness, life vest, daylight only, avoid narrow overgrown caños solo","si":"RCR/GEA","blurb":"Can be unguided but guide advised Caiman & crocodile awareness, life vest, daylight only, avoid narrow overgrown caños solo","when":"Jul-Aug  into Sep-Oct","commission":"lodge activity add-on / local operator affiliate"},{"name":"Cerro Tortuguero viewpoint hike","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://vamosrentacar.com/blog/tortuguero-national-park-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Guided or self Trail footing, heat/humidity, hydration; separate park sector ticket","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided or self Trail footing, heat/humidity, hydration; separate park sector ticket","when":"year-round","commission":"guided-hike add-on (separate sector ticket)"},{"name":"Sea Turtle Conservancy visitor center","si_tag":"Culture/Conservation","tier":"essential","source":"https://conserveturtles.org/project/stc-programs-research-tortuguero-costa-rica/","si":"Culture/Conservation","commission":"conservation donation + guided-visit add-on"},{"name":"Tortuguero village + Afro-Caribbean culture","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.twoweeksincostarica.com/sea-turtle-conservancy-tortuguero/","timing":"Jul-Aug  into Sep-Oct","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Jul-Aug  into Sep-Oct","commission":"village-stay bedbank + local F&B/tour affiliate"}],"faq":[{"q":"When do turtles nest in Tortuguero?","a":"Green turtles — the peak draw — nest July 1–October 15, concentrated Jul–Oct with highest activity Jul–Aug, and hatchlings emerge Sep–Oct (~60 days post-lay). The rarer leatherback window is Feb–Apr. Book weeks ahead, since tour slots are lottery-capped at 15 per visit.","source":"tortugueronationalpark.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"What wildlife will you see on a Tortuguero canal safari?","a":"A lot: the canal network holds 442 bird species, 138 mammals and 118 reptiles, and a dawn boat safari routinely turns up spider, howler and capuchin monkeys, keel-billed toucans, tiger herons, spectacled caimans, three-toed sloths and river otters.","source":"entercostarica.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"How do you get to Tortuguero?","a":"By water, always — there is no passable road to the village. Arrive by boat via La Pavona or Moín, or fly the 25-min SJO→TTQ small-strip flight and finish by boat transfer. The boat isn''t a transfer detail here; it''s the whole mode of travel and touring.","source":"frommers.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"river"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in a boat-only jungle?","a":"Remoteness and water. The nearest mainland hospital is in Guápiles, with San José for major trauma, and ambulances don''t reach here within standard windows — serious cases need boat + road/air evacuation. Do not swim: caimans and crocodiles patrol the canals, and the beach surf carries dangerous rip currents.","source":"internationalinsurance.com, 2026-07-06 · vamosrentacar.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What are the rules on the night turtle-nesting walk?","a":"A certified park guide is legally required — this is the one activity where a guide is the law, not a suggestion. Tours run 7–10 pm, are capped at 15 people, and demand red-light only (no white light or flash) and dark, non-reflective clothing; stay behind the guide throughout.","source":"tortugueronationalpark.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Tortuguero, Costa Rica: Sea-Turtle Nesting & the Little Amazon Canal Safari","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"es-CR","local_keywords":["Parque Nacional Tortuguero","tortugas Tortuguero","tour canales Tortuguero","temporada de desove tortuga verde","cómo llegar a Tortuguero en lancha","avistamiento de tortugas guiado"],"hreflang":["en","es-CR"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","river"],"ultra":[{"property":"Tortuga Lodge & Gardens","management":"Böÿ Hotels (historically Cayuga Collection)","tier":"ultra_eco_ceiling","consortia":"Fora advisor lane; Virtuoso status unconfirmed — verify","mor":"highest in-destination","note":"146 private acres, 27 rooms incl. suites + penthouse, riverfront; no palace-ultra exists at Tortuguero"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Tortuguero, Costa Rica"},"geo":{"lat":10.5432,"lng":-83.5041}}'::jsonb, 114),
  ('tulum-mexico', '10S', 'Tulum', 'Mexico', 'Cliff-top Maya ruins and cenote diving', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Quintana Roo (Cancún & Riviera Maya)', '{"expedition","diveglobal","culture","wildlife"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Tulum ruins are the only Maya walled city built on a seaside cliff (El Castillo, Temple of the Frescoes).","Tulum sits above Sistema Sac Actun, a ~347 km interconnected underwater cave system.","Archaeological zone: 8am-5pm, last entry 3:30pm; best 8-10am.","Sian Ka''an Biosphere Reserve (UNESCO) borders the destination to the south.","Tulum''s open Atlantic-facing beaches are the worst-hit by sargassum in the Riviera Maya."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Nearest trauma: Hospiten Riviera Maya, Playa del Carmen (+52 984 159 2200), ~60 km north; local clinics stabilize/transfer; major trauma to Cancún","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"none in tourist Quintana Roo","yellow_fever":"none required","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Apr (dry season)","shoulder":"Nov & Feb (best value inside peak)","green":"Apr-Oct (heat, hurricane Jun-Nov, sargassum Apr-Aug)","price_swing_peak_pct":"40-60% above shoulder","shoulder_discount_pct":"15-25% below peak","booking_lead":{"christmas_nye":"reserve by September (Dec 20-Jan 5 fully books; NYE is the flagship premium window)","feb_mar_peak":"book by November (incl. Spring Break + Holy Week 2026 Mar 29-Apr 5)"},"holiday_event_peaks":["New Year''s Eve","Christmas week","Holy Week 2026-03-29/2026-04-05","Spring Break (March)"],"out_of_season_fill":"Apr-Oct: sell ruins/cenotes/Sian Ka''an, not a beach promise; cenote diving is weather-independent + sargassum-immune","campaign_start_trigger":"NYE/Christmas by mid-August; Feb-Mar peak by early October; Apr-Aug campaigns must not promise pristine beach (sargassum guardrail)","source":"https://casatira.com/best-time-to-visit-tulum-month-by-month-weather-crowd-guide-for-2026"},"jewels":[{"name":"Dos Ojos cavern dive (Sistema Sac Actun)","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","hook":"Guided cavern dives with cathedral light in the world''s longest cave system.","bookable_category":"cenote cave/cavern dive (guide required)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-tulum/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"Guided cavern dives with cathedral light in the world''s longest cave system.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"Amstar 12% / affiliate 4-8%"},{"name":"Gran Cenote snorkel/intro dive","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Crystal-clear cenote with turtles and stalactites, all ages and levels.","bookable_category":"cenote tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-tulum/","si":"expedition","blurb":"Crystal-clear cenote with turtles and stalactites, all ages and levels.","commission":"Amstar 12%; entry pass-through"},{"name":"Tulum ruins at opening light","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Cliff-top Maya walled city with sea views no other Maya site can match.","bookable_category":"guided cultural excursion","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/tulum-ruins-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Cliff-top Maya walled city with sea views no other Maya site can match.","when":"year-round","commission":"Amstar 12%; ruin entry pass-through"},{"name":"Cobá jungle pyramids","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Taller jungle-clad Maya pyramids explorable by bike, ~28 mi north.","bookable_category":"guided cultural excursion","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-tulum/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Taller jungle-clad Maya pyramids explorable by bike, ~28 mi north.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"Amstar 12% / affiliate"},{"name":"Sian Ka''an Biosphere Reserve","si_tag":"Wildlife & Nature","status":"future","hook":"UNESCO biosphere lagoon float — an eco-safari and a sargassum-proof day.","bookable_category":"eco-tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-tulum/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wildlife","blurb":"UNESCO biosphere lagoon float — an eco-safari and a sargassum-proof day.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"affiliate 4-8% / DMC 12%; biosphere fee pass-through"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Tulum?","a":"Sargassum above all — Tulum is the worst-hit beach stretch on the Riviera Maya, and 2026 is a record year, so beach quality is genuinely not guaranteed. Anchor the trip on ruins, cenotes and Sian Ka''an rather than a pristine-beach promise. Also plan for hurricane season (Jun–Nov), bottled water, and dengue (peak May–Nov, no malaria).","source":"deeparrival.com / cdc.gov, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is cenote and cave diving in Tulum dangerous?","a":"It demands the right certification for serious overhead-environment diving. Sistema Sac Actun and Dos Ojos are caves: cavern diving requires a certified cave/cavern guide and must stay in the daylight zone, and the dark cave zone requires full cave certification — no exceptions, no solo penetration. Observe no-fly of 18h single / 24h repetitive; the nearest chamber is ~60 km north.","source":"sssnetwork.com / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When should I visit the Tulum ruins?","a":"Right at the 8am opening. The archaeological zone runs 8am–5pm (last entry 3:30pm), and the 8–10am window beats both the heat and the crowds at this cliff-top walled city. Come in November or February for low crowds and ideal temperatures; Holy Week (2026: Mar 29–Apr 5) runs at full capacity and Apr–Oct heat is intense.","source":"absolute-adventure-mexico.com / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What are the best cenotes for diving near Tulum?","a":"Gran Cenote and Dos Ojos lead — Tulum sits above Sistema Sac Actun, a ~347 km interconnected cave system, the densest cenote country in Mexico. Gran Cenote (2.5 mi from town) is an all-levels swim/snorkel/intro-dive; Dos Ojos is the marquee guided cavern dive. All are weather-independent and sargassum-immune, making them the reliable core of a Tulum trip.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Will sargassum ruin the Tulum beaches in 2026?","a":"Be realistic: Tulum is the worst-hit stretch on the coast, its open Atlantic-facing beaches catch the full brunt, and 2026 is a record/near-record year — beach quality is not guaranteed. Don''t cancel; re-anchor. Build the trip on ruins, cenotes and the Sian Ka''an biosphere (all sargassum-proof), and for reliable sand, the Punta Maroma stretch ~1 hour north sits north of the worst.","source":"deeparrival.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"What is Tulum''s wellness scene like?","a":"It is Tulum''s defining draw — yoga, temazcal ceremonies, cenote healing and jungle spas concentrated along the beach road. A signature is a north-Tulum cove with a beachfront cenote where you swim fresh and salt water in one spot, paired with jungle wellness. Book through a boutique hotel or DMC; some of the best programs are direct-only.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"wellness"},{"q":"Is Tulum good for a honeymoon, and where''s the luxury?","a":"Yes — it is a honeymoon icon, built on bohemian-luxe boutiques and staffed villas. On the beach road, design icons like Azulik and Our Habitas Tulum lead (many are direct-only — verify the channel); for branded ultra beyond the sargassum, Maroma (A Belmond Hotel) and the 70-villa Chablé Maroma sit ~1 hour north. Fully staffed beach villas are the top private rung.","source":"virtuoso.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Tulum, and how far ahead do I book?","a":"November–April is the dry high season; November and February are the best value inside it (roughly 15–25% below peak), with November the single best month (dry, minimal seaweed, pre-holiday prices). Peak weeks run 40–60% above shoulder — reserve Christmas/NYE by September and Feb–March by November, as the boutique scene sells out months ahead.","source":"casatira.com / boldlygo.world, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Tulum Travel Guide 2026 — Maya Ruins, Cenotes, Sian Ka''an & Straight Sargassum | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Tulum: cliff-top Maya ruins at dawn, Sistema Sac Actun cenote diving, Sian Ka''an biosphere, plus straight 2026 sargassum reality, Level 2 safety and dive-chamber contacts.","slug":"tulum-mexico","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["ruinas de Tulum horarios","mejor época para visitar Tulum","cenotes Tulum buceo","sargazo Tulum 2026","Sian Ka''an tour","villas de lujo Tulum","hoteles boutique Tulum"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Maroma, A Belmond Hotel","what":"Iconic Punta Maroma beach resort, reimagined 2023, ~1h north of Tulum","why_ultra":"Belmond/LVMH flag, best regional beach north of Tulum sargassum zone","earning":"agent/consortium — on application via host-Virtuoso","virtuoso":"Virtuoso-listed (upgrade, breakfast, ~$100-200 credit, early/late)","mor":"consortium-rack — safe (green)","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.virtuoso.com/travel/luxury-hotels/6163634/maroma-a-belmond-hotel-riviera-maya"},{"name":"Chablé Maroma","what":"70 pool-villa wellness retreat on Punta Maroma, cenote spa","why_ultra":"Destination-spa ultra, private-pool villas","earning":"agent/consortium — on application via host-Virtuoso","virtuoso":"Virtuoso-listed (VIP amenities)","mor":"consortium-rack — safe (green)","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.virtuoso.com/travel/luxury-hotels/15885219/chable-maroma"},{"name":"Azulik Tulum","what":"Adults-only treehouse eco villas, candlelit, cenote-fed baths, Tulum beach road","why_ultra":"Singular design icon, definitive Tulum eco-ultra (polarizing)","earning":"verify — largely direct-only; on application","virtuoso":"not confirmed — treat as direct-only, flag","mor":"amber — confirm booking channel before quoting commission","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://travel.usnews.com/hotels/review-azulik_-_adults_eco-resort_maya_spa-tulum-mexico-27488/"},{"name":"Casa Malca","what":"Former Pablo Escobar beachfront mansion, art-filled boutique hotel, Tulum beach road","why_ultra":"One-of-one provenance + curated art; boutique-ultra scarcity","earning":"on application — many beach-road boutiques direct-only; verify channel","virtuoso":"verify listing","mor":"amber — direct-only risk, confirm before net-rate","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://casamalca.com/"},{"name":"Our Habitas Tulum","what":"Adults-only canvas-and-wood beachfront eco sanctuary, quiet Tulum beach road, reef-regeneration program","why_ultra":"Design-forward luxe-eco with strong wellness/community program","earning":"on application via host / brand TA program","virtuoso":"on Visa Signature / Mr & Mrs Smith — verify Virtuoso","mor":"confirm channel — amber","price_tier":"luxury-ultra","source":"https://www.ourhabitas.com/tulum/"},{"name":"Staffed ultra villas — Tulum beach road","what":"Fully-staffed multi-bedroom beachfront villas (e.g. 10-BR Villa Privada), chef + concierge","why_ultra":"Buy-out privacy, staffed service, direct beach access — top villa rung","earning":"commissionable via villa specialist (VOD / Journey Mexico / Isle Blue / Loco Luxury)","virtuoso":"via villa-consortium programs","mor":"commissionable-rack = safe (green); net-rate resale = flag red","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.loco.luxury/villaprivada"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Tulum, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.2114,"lng":-87.4654}}'::jsonb, 115),
  ('utila-honduras', '10S', 'Utila', 'Honduras', 'Utila Honduras diving', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Honduras', '{"liveaboard","tropical","expedition"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["World''s cheapest PADI/SSI Open Water cert (~US$280-350), free/discounted dorm while diving; 60+ dive sites on the Mesoamerican Barrier Reef (2nd-largest on Earth)","Whale sharks year-round (best Mar-May + Aug-Sep); snorkel-only from the surface - scuba diving WITH whale sharks is prohibited","Reached by air to Roatan (RTB) or San Pedro Sula (SAP) + ferry from La Ceiba (~1 hr, ~US$35, Utila Dream ferry - sole operator); Utila airstrip is private-charter only","Budget-to-boutique dive island; ceiling = dive-resort lodge (Utila Lodge 8 over-water rooms, Mango Inn); NO branded ultra on-island - Roatan/Guanaja hold the luxury tier","The Cays / Water Cay uninhabited white-sand sandbar (Sun Jam festival site); Utila Cays Garifuna fishing village (Jewel + Pigeon/Suc-Suc); Chepes Beach; endangered Utila spiny-tailed iguana station"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (national police/fire/ambulance, Honduras - verify locally)","hyperbaric_chamber":"ON-ISLAND - Utila has its own chamber (at Utila Lodge, also doubling as island trauma center; a chamber also via Bay Islands College of Diving/College of Diving); a genuine asset most small dive islands lack","no_fly_after_diving":true,"hospital":"small clinics only + the Utila Lodge hyperbaric/trauma center on-island; serious trauma/complex dive cases route OFF-ISLAND to La Ceiba (mainland) then mainland hospital or US medevac; carry travel-medical + air-evac + DAN dive insurance","remote_flag":true,"book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"state_dept_carveout":"Bay Islands (Roatan/Utila/Guanaja) explicitly noted by State as better-policed resource-concentration areas; Gracias a Dios Dept = Level 4 Do Not Travel (isolated eastern mainland); danger is mainland, away from Utila","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":"RTB (Roatan) or SAP (San Pedro Sula) international arrival, then ferry to Utila from La Ceiba (~1 hr, ~US$35, Utila Dream ferry) or Roatan-Utila ferry; Utila airstrip = private charter only; routing never touches mainland gang zones","reef_safety":"protected Mesoamerican marine reserve - no-touch/no-stand, reef-safe sunscreen; wall/deep-site currents; whale-shark no-touch/no-scuba boat protocol","dengue":"dengue occasionally reported on Utila - protect against daytime Aedes (DEET/picaridin)","sandfly":"sandflies/no-see-ums are the signature nuisance, most active dusk-to-dawn; standard DEET underperforms - use oil-based lotion (Skin So Soft), cover up, net/fan at night; bites rarely carry leishmaniasis","water":"tap water NOT potable - bottled/refill only; mind ice/raw produce; wash hands before eating"},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Apr (dry season; Christmas-New Year + Easter/Semana Santa sub-peaks)","whale_shark_subpeaks":"Mar-May and Aug-Sep (year-round presence; best odds; Aug-Sep is a green-season demand spike)","shoulder_green":"late-Oct-mid/late-Feb rains + Sep-Oct highest storm risk (value trough; but Sep is a whale-shark sub-peak); value island stays busy with cert traffic","booking_window_lead_time":"TWO SPEEDS - dive-cert/backpacker = short-lead (days-to-weeks, walk-in dorms, rolling last-minute layer); over-water dive-lodge tier + peak whale-shark weeks + Christmas/Easter = 2-4 months ahead","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"dive-cert value packages, Aug-Sep whale-shark spike at shoulder rates, freediving courses (weather-resilient), new-moon night dives, Cays day-trips between storms","holiday_event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, Easter/Semana Santa, Sun Jam (Water Cay, ~August - verify dates), whale-shark sub-peaks as de-facto events","fire_date":"dry-peak: early-to-mid November (curve-start late-Nov minus 1-2 wks); Mar-May whale-shark: mid-February; Aug-Sep whale-shark: mid-July; dive-cert stays book-short-lead with permanent rolling last-minute layer","flag":"whale-shark sightings are probabilistic - market ''best odds'' never a guarantee; sharpen dates on live booking-pace tracking","dive_calendar":true,"sources":["https://www.utilalodge.com/whale-shark-encounters","https://www.islaguru.com/articles/utila-travel-practical-guide","https://www.mango-inn.com/","https://www.freediveutila.com/"]},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"liveaboard","name":"PADI/SSI Open Water certification (world''s cheapest)","why":"~US$280-350, free dorm while diving; the entry drug that turns a 3-day stop into a 3-week stay","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"essential","source":"https://utiladivecenter.com/","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"dive-operator commission on application; CLIA dive-lane convert to commissioned agent"},{"si_tag":"liveaboard","name":"Night dive - ''string of pearls'' bioluminescence (Ted''s Point / Ron''s Wreck)","why":"kill the lights on a new moon and watch ostracod bioluminescence flash through the water column; hunting octopus","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.dive-utila.com/advanced-open-water-diver","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"dive-operator + CLIA lane"},{"si_tag":"liveaboard","name":"Halliburton wreck + Airport Caves (deep/wall)","why":"upright cargo-ship wreck ~30 m + cavern swim-throughs full of glassy sweepers - the reef''s set-pieces","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.dive-utila.com/advanced-open-water-diver","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"dive-operator + CLIA lane"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Whale-shark snorkel expedition","why":"snorkel beside the largest fish in the ocean, year-round; captains hunt the bait-ball boil + diving birds","timing":"year-round; peak odds Mar-May + Aug-Sep","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.utilalodge.com/whale-shark-encounters","si":"expedition","when":"year-round; peak odds Mar-May + Aug-Sep","commission":"operator/expedition commission on application + Viator/GYG affiliate; CLIA-lane crossover"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Freediving course (Freedive Utila - Central America''s freediving HQ)","why":"learn to fall through the blue on one breath at the region''s only competitive freediving cooperative","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.freediveutila.com/","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"course commission on application"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Utila Iguana Station (endangered spiny-tailed ''swamper'' iguana)","why":"conservation center for the iguana found only on Utila, living in its mangroves - a meaningful low-cost morning","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.islaguru.com/articles/things-to-do-utila-island-honduras","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"non-commissionable conservation donation - value-add/character stop, not a margin line"},{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"Water Cay (the Cays) day-trip","why":"tiny uninhabited white-sand island + sandbar ringed by coral; snorkel-and-sandbar paradise; Sun Jam festival site","timing":"year-round, calm-day best; festival ~August","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.utilawatersport.com/water-cay","si":"tropical","when":"year-round, calm-day best; festival ~August","commission":"local boat/tour operator + Viator affiliate (marine-park fee non-commissionable)"},{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"Utila Cays - Jewel Cay & Pigeon (Suc-Suc) Garifuna fishing village","why":"two cays joined by a footbridge, ~500 people on stilt homes over the water - a Garifuna/Caymanian fishing-village time capsule","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.utilaguide.com/activities/cays/","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"local boat operator + F&B affiliate-adjacent"},{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"Chepes Beach + Rehab bar","why":"the island''s largest public beach - soft white sand, shallow calm water, beachfront bar; the free between-dives afternoon","timing":"year-round","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.islaguru.com/articles/things-to-do-utila-island-honduras","si":"tropical","when":"year-round","commission":"F&B/OTA-adjacent scene-setter, not a margin line"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Two risks are load-bearing: mainland crime and island remoteness. The advisory names Gracias a Dios Department (Level 4 \"Do Not Travel\") and urban mainland gang zones — all away from Utila, so keep the client in-zone (airport → ferry/charter → island). Separately, serious trauma or complex dive injuries route off-island to La Ceiba then a mainland hospital or US medevac, so carry travel-medical, air-evac, and DAN dive insurance without exception.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2024-12-10","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is learning to dive here dangerous, and can I fly out afterward?","a":"Diving here rewards a certified operator and disciplined profiles, and Utila has an unusual on-island safety asset. Certify only with a PADI/SSI-certified shop (UDC, Alton''s, Parrots, College of Diving, Underwater Vision), dive within no-decompression limits, and observe no-fly-after-diving of 18–24 hours before flying. Utila has its own hyperbaric chamber at Utila Lodge (doubling as the island trauma center), with a chamber also via Bay Islands College of Diving — a genuine asset most small dive islands lack.","source":"utilalodge.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Why is Utila the cheapest place to learn to dive?","a":"Utila built its name as the place backpackers came to get certified for a few hundred dollars and never left. A PADI/SSI Open Water course runs roughly US$280–350 — among the cheapest on Earth — with free or discounted dorm accommodation while you dive, on a reef with 60+ dive sites a few fin-kicks off the dock.","source":"alongdustyroads.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"Can I dive with the whale sharks, or only snorkel?","a":"Snorkel only — scuba diving with whale sharks is prohibited. As a protected species they are approached from the surface during surface intervals: captains hunt the \"boil/roil\" of feeding fish and diving birds, and you drop off the boat and snorkel beside them. Sightings are probabilistic (best odds Mar–May and Aug–Sep) — market \"best odds,\" never a guarantee.","source":"utilalodge.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What is there to do on Utila besides diving?","a":"Plenty above the water, all budget-friendly. Take a boat to Water Cay''s uninhabited white-sand sandbar, cold cans at Chepes Beach (the island''s largest public beach), the Utila Cays Garífuna fishing village of Jewel Cay and Pigeon (~500 people on stilt homes over the water), and Freedive Utila — Central America''s first freediving training center — where you learn to fall through the blue on one breath.","source":"islaguru.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Utila Honduras: Cheapest Dive Certs + Whale Sharks Year-Round","meta_description":"Get PADI-certified for ~$300, snorkel with year-round whale sharks, and explore Water Cay and the Mesoamerican reef — Utila is Honduras''s budget-to-boutique dive island. When to go, how to get there, and how to stay safe.","slug":"utila-honduras","primary_keyword":"Utila Honduras diving","long_tail":["cheapest PADI certification Utila","whale sharks Utila snorkel season","how to get to Utila from Roatan La Ceiba ferry","Utila vs Roatan diving budget","Water Cay Utila day trip","Freedive Utila freediving course","Utila hyperbaric chamber dive safety"],"search_language":"es-HN","local_keywords":["buceo Utila","tiburón ballena Utila","curso de buceo Utila","certificación PADI Utila barato","cómo llegar a Utila desde La Ceiba","Cayos de Utila / Water Cay","apnea Utila (freediving)"],"hreflang":["en","es-HN"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"liveaboard","status":"live"},{"si":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Private dive charter / private liveaboard day (out of Utila)","location":"on-Utila waters","posture":"the on-island ultra move is exclusivity on the water, not a hotel - private boat/guide/whale-shark hunt","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"local operator + David''s CLIA dive lane - convert to commissioned agent where offered","mor":"commissionable only where offered; no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.utilalodge.com/"},{"name":"Roatan luxury base (branded/boutique + dive-luxury lodges)","location":"neighboring Bay Island (short ferry/flight)","posture":"the Bay Islands'' actual luxury tier - route ultra client to a Roatan base, day/overnight to Utila for whale sharks","price_tier":"ultra/luxury","earning":"Fora / host-Virtuoso lane - commission on application","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/traveladvisories/traveladvisories/honduras-travel-advisory.html"},{"name":"Guanaja private-island seclusion","location":"third/quietest Bay Island","posture":"small exclusive private-island/eco-luxury lodges - the no-crowds seclusion play","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"Fora / host-Virtuoso / CLIA - on application","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.utilaguide.com/general/utilafaqs/"},{"name":"Utila on-island lodging","posture":"STATED PLAINLY: NO branded ultra on Utila; ceiling = comfortable dive-resort lodge (Utila Lodge / Mango Inn); sell as the whale-shark + dive day to a Roatan/Guanaja ultra base or a private charter","price_tier":"premier (ceiling)","earning":"n/a for ultra","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.utilalodge.com/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-07","hero":{"query":"Utila, Honduras"},"geo":{"lat":16.0983,"lng":-86.935}}'::jsonb, 116)
