  ('uxmal-mexico', '10S', 'Uxmal', 'Mexico', '*If it''s a city the Maya built for the', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Yucatán (Mérida & Chichén Itzá)', '{"culture","expedition","culinary"}', '{}', '{"comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["UNESCO World Heritage since 1996; Puuc-style Maya capital, flourished 7th-10th c. AD, regional capital c. 850-950 AD","Pyramid of the Magician ~35m/100ft, rounded-corner, five build-phases, solstice-aligned; climbing banned","Open daily 8:00-17:00 (last entry ~16:00); 2026 foreign admission 556 MXN (95 INAH + 461 State)","Ecos de Uxmal light-and-sound show (4K video mapping, 2026), foreign ~748 MXN, Tue/Wed/Fri-Sun","~78 km / ~1h14 south of Mérida via Hwy 261 — a Mérida day-trip; anchor of the Ruta Puuc (Kabah, Sayil, Labná, Xlapak, Loltún)"],"safety":{"emergency_number":"911","nearest_trauma":"Mérida (~1h15 north; regional hospital hub)","advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"MID Mérida ~1h15 drive; US nonstops incl. Houston, Miami, Dallas, Atlanta","primary_hazards":["heat/sun exposure (unshaded limestone plazas)","remote Puuc route with limited services","Loltún cave footing (guided-only)","steep Maya risers on Great Pyramid climb","dengue (rainy season)","non-potable tap water"],"climbing_note":"El Adivino climbing BANNED; Great Pyramid climbable north side","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"2026-11-01","peak":"2026-12 to 2027-04","shoulder":"2026-05 to 2026-10 (hot/humid; hurricane exposure Aug-Oct)","fire_date":"2026-10-22","trigger_rule":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks; attaches to Mérida-base lead time","booking_lead_days":{"day_tour":"2-7","merida_base_high_season":"28-84"},"event_peaks":["Hanal Pixán / Day of the Dead 2026-10-31 to 2026-11-02","summer solstice El Adivino alignment","evening light-and-sound show (dry-cool nights)"],"selling_point":"markedly less crowded than Chichén Itzá","note":"sharpen on live tracking — Mérida occupancy curves + INAH visitor counts"},"jewels":[{"name":"Pyramid of the Magician (El Adivino)","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/blog/uxmal | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culture","commission":"bundled in day-tour (guiding+transport, Host)","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Nunnery Quadrangle","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/blog/uxmal | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culture","commission":"day-tour inclusion","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Governor''s Palace","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/blog/uxmal | Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"day-tour + private-guide upsell","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Ecos de Uxmal light-and-sound show","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/uxmal-light-sound-show-2026-evening-experience-guide.htm | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culture","commission":"non-commissionable ticket; drives Mérida-base room-nights","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Kabah — Codz Poop (Palace of Masks, ~250 Chaac masks)","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","source":"https://worldhistoryedu.com/kabah-history-and-major-facts-of-this-maya-archaeological-site/ | Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"private Puuc day-tour extension","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Sayil — Grand Palace (3-story, 100+ columns)","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/ruta-puuc-2026-kabah-sayil-labna-uxmal-circuit.htm | Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"Puuc day-tour extension","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Labná — Arch of Labná","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/ruta-puuc-2026-kabah-sayil-labna-uxmal-circuit.htm | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culture","commission":"Puuc day-tour extension","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Xlapak","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"premier","source":"https://en-yucatan.com/ruta-puuc/ | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culture","commission":"completes premium private Ruta Puuc itinerary","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Loltún caves (700m+ guided)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/lolt-n-caves/ | Accessed 2026-07-06","hook":"Uneven, sometimes slick underground surfaces over a 700m+ route; entry is guided-only for safety","si":"expedition","blurb":"Uneven, sometimes slick underground surfaces over a 700m+ route; entry is guided-only for safety","commission":"GEA add-on (guiding/transport, Host); entrance non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Choco-Story México (Ecomuseo del Cacao)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/blog/choco-story-uxmal-an-interactive-museum | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culinary","commission":"add-on ticket (affiliate/Viator) + lunch upsell","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Hacienda Yaxcopoil","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.beyondtheordinary.co.uk/features/hacienda-yaxcopoil/ | Accessed 2026-07-06","hook":"19th-C henequen estate turned atmospheric museum, on Hwy 261 en route to Uxmal; visitable and event-capable","si":"culture","blurb":"19th-C henequen estate turned atmospheric museum, on Hwy 261 en route to Uxmal; visitable and event-capable","commission":"visit add-on; private-event via Host","accessed":"2026-07-06"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Uxmal worth visiting instead of Chichén Itzá?","a":"Yes — it is the connoisseur''s Maya city. Uxmal is markedly less crowded than Chichén Itzá, with grander Puuc-style architecture: the rounded-corner Pyramid of the Magician, the lattice-stone Nunnery Quadrangle, and a Governor''s Palace whose five-acre platform carries an extended Chaac mosaic frieze. UNESCO inscribed it in 1996.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Can you climb the pyramid at Uxmal?","a":"Partly — the distinction matters. Climbing El Adivino (the Pyramid of the Magician) is banned to protect it, but the Great Pyramid is climbable on its north side, on steep handrail-free Maya risers, so wear sturdy shoes and mind your footing. Do not assume the iconic rounded pyramid can be summited.","source":"yucatantoday.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What is the Ruta Puuc, and are the Loltún caves worth it?","a":"The Ruta Puuc is the backroad ruin circuit south of Uxmal — Kabah (whose Codz Poop wears ~250 interlocking Chaac masks), Sayil''s three-story palace, the photogenic Arch of Labná, and quiet Xlapak. The Loltún caves cap it: a 700 m+ guided-only underground walk past cave paintings and \"musical\" ringing columns. A guided day neutralizes the heat, the remote road and the mandatory cave guide in one wrapper.","source":"yucatantoday.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Uxmal and on the Puuc route?","a":"Heat and remoteness, not crime. Uxmal''s plazas are fully exposed limestone with almost no shade, and the Ruta Puuc runs long stretches with no fuel, water or medical services between sites. Time the visit for early morning or late afternoon, carry 1.5–2 L of water per person plus a hat and SPF, and leave Muna with a full tank; the nearest hospital is Mérida, ~1h15 north.","source":"yucatantoday.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"jsonld_type":"TouristAttraction","meta_title":"Uxmal & the Ruta Puuc: UNESCO Maya City Guide (2026) | TravelWell.World","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Uxmal Ruta Puuc","Pirámide del Adivino","espectáculo de luz y sonido Uxmal","Grutas de Loltún visita guiada","haciendas Ruta Puuc","Kabah Codz Poop"],"long_tail_en":["Uxmal ruins guide 2026","Uxmal from Mérida day trip","Ruta Puuc Kabah Sayil Labná itinerary","Uxmal light and sound show tickets","Uxmal vs Chichén Itzá less crowded"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["culture_heritage","expedition","culinary"],"ultra":[{"name":"Chablé Yucatán","tier":"ultra","earning_path":"Virtuoso / Fora","note":"#13 World''s Best Hotels 2023; 3,400+ tequila bottles; ~30 min Mérida","source":"https://www.virtuoso.com/travel/luxury-hotels/15452675/chable-yucatan | Accessed 2026-07-06"},{"name":"Hacienda Temozón (Luxury Collection)","tier":"ultra","earning_path":"Virtuoso / Marriott STARS / Fora / MoR","note":"28 rooms; ~35 min Uxmal — natural Puuc base","source":"https://www.travelweekly.com/Hotels/Abala-Mexico/Hacienda-Temozon-Luxury-Collection-p51093491 | Accessed 2026-07-06"},{"name":"Hacienda Santa Rosa (Luxury Collection)","tier":"ultra","earning_path":"Virtuoso / Marriott STARS / MoR","note":"intimate 11 rooms","source":"https://www.letstraveltomexico.com/yucatan-haciendas/ | Accessed 2026-07-06"},{"name":"The Lodge at Uxmal","tier":"premier","earning_path":"Host FIT / MoR","note":"on-gate, walk to ruins"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Uxmal, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.3597,"lng":-89.7714}}'::jsonb, 117),
  ('valladolid-mexico', '10S', 'Valladolid', 'Mexico', 'Valladolid Yucatán', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Yucatán (Mérida & Chichén Itzá)', '{"expedition","culture","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["1543 colonial city + Pueblo Magico (2012), ~150 km from both Merida and Cancun; mid-peninsula base","Cenote Zaci in the heart of town (short staircase, park); swimmable, free w/ ~100 MXN restaurant","Cenote Suytun ~5 km E - iconic single light-beam on stone platform ~1-3 PM; ~250 MXN (230 online), 9 AM-5 PM","Cenote Oxman on a working hacienda - deep sinkhole + roots + rope swing + pool; 150 MXN (350 w/ lunch)","Ek Balam ~30 min N - CLIMBABLE 32 m acropolis (unlike Chichen), intricate stucco; ~170 MXN cash only"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"basic hospitals in town; nearest full trauma care Merida (~2 hr W, Star Medica/Clinica de Merida) or Cancun (~2 hr E, Hospiten/Amerimed) or air-evac","advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":"yes - ~2 hr from MID Merida and ~2 hr from CUN Cancun (~150 km from each)","heat":"intense Yucatan sun - visit cenotes/Ek Balam at 9 AM opening; carry water + SPF; heat exhaustion risk at open ruins","cenote":"Zaci/Suytun/Oxman = swim/snorkel, NO lifeguard; life jackets (mandatory posture for non-swimmers/children); shower off sunscreen; slick platforms (Suytun) + rope swing (Oxman) - jump only where directed","dive_spine":"DISTINGUISH swim/snorkel (no cert) vs GUIDED cavern dive (certified cavern guide, light zone) vs CAVE dive (TECHNICAL - full cave cert, overhead, silt-out - FLAG HARD, never blur). Yucatan = world''s longest flooded caves (Ox-Bel-Ha ~269 km)","hyperbaric_no_fly":"nearest chambers on coast ~2+ hr (SSS/DAN Cancun, Playa, Cozumel; SSS Merida ~2 hr W); interior Yucatan has NO adjacent chamber - multi-hour evac for cave/cavern diving; DAN = nearest hospital first; observe no-fly 18-24 hr after multi-day/repetitive dives; carry DAN insurance","malaria":"effectively none in tourist zone","dengue":"active in Yucatan 2026; chikungunya/Zika circulate - use repellent","water":"bottled/purified only","hurricane":"Jun-Nov","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"late September (winter/dry-season beds harden for Nov-Apr) / early February (Chichen spring-equinox halo)","peak":"dry season Nov-Apr; acute spikes = Chichen spring-equinox halo ~Mar 20-21 (closest boutique-bed base) + Dia de Muertos/Hanal Pixan late Oct-Nov 2","fire_date":"2026-09-14 (winter/dry-season campaign) and 2027-01-25 (spring-equinox halo push) - both curve-start minus 1-2 wks","shoulder":"May + Oct","green":"Jun-Sep (heat/humidity peak, hurricane-season afternoon rain) - cenotes at 9 AM opening","booking_lead":"boutique/casona beds weeks-to-months for Nov-Apr; equinox halo + Dia de Muertos = tight, book months ahead; cenote/Ek Balam/Cuzama tours on-site or a day out","off_season_specials":"green window: position as cool-off cenote base (Zaci/Suytun/Oxman + Cuzama/Homun) + slow-travel colonial alt to hot coast; bundle guided cavern-dive intro","event_peaks":"Dia de Muertos/Hanal Pixan (late Oct-Nov 2) = signature cultural peak; Chichen spring-equinox halo ~Mar 20-21; Semana Santa; Christmas-New Year","note":"sharpen on live tracking - confirm 2026 Hanal Pixan dates + 2027 equinox date; boutique inventory thin, sells out","sources":["https://www.lugaresturisticosenmexico.com/en/valladolid-yucatan-pueblo-magico/","https://thehaphazardtraveler.com/valladolid-yucatan-mexico/","https://www.dreambigtravelfarblog.com/blog/cenote-suytun"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Cenote Zací (in-town)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"entry on site (free w/ ~100 MXN restaurant) + combo tour","source":"https://cenotesworld.com/en/cenotes-in-Valladolid-Pueblo-Magico-Yucatan/Cenote-Zaci/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a swimmable sinkhole a 2-min walk from the main square, in a public park; the only in-town cenote, gentlest first-swim","si":"expedition","blurb":"a swimmable sinkhole a 2-min walk from the main square, in a public park; the only in-town cenote, gentlest first-swim","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate (entry non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Cenote Suytun (iconic light-beam)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"entry ~250 MXN (230 online) + combo tour","source":"https://www.dreambigtravelfarblog.com/blog/cenote-suytun","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the region''s most photographed cenote — a single beam of light falls on a central stone platform","si":"expedition","blurb":"the region''s most photographed cenote — a single beam of light falls on a central stone platform","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Cenote Oxman (hacienda sinkhole + rope swing)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"150 MXN (350 w/ pool + lunch)","source":"https://cenotefinder.com/cenotes-in-mexico/valladolid-cenotes/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"deep sinkhole draped in roots on a working hacienda, pool + restaurant, quieter","si":"expedition","blurb":"deep sinkhole draped in roots on a working hacienda, pool + restaurant, quieter","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Cuzamá / Homún cenote country (horse-cart route)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"on-site cart ~400 MXN (up to 4) + guided day tour; vet operator for animal welfare","source":"https://www.offpathtravels.com/cenotes-cuzama/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"three-cenote railway horse-cart route through the meteor-crater Ring of Cenotes; Homún offers gentler truck/bike alternatives — vet operator for animal welfare","si":"expedition","blurb":"three-cenote railway horse-cart route through the meteor-crater Ring of Cenotes; Homún offers gentler truck/bike alternatives — vet operator for animal welfare","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Guided cavern dive base","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable":"professional cave/cavern dive operator (certified guide)","source":"https://travelyucatan.com/cave-and-cenote-diving/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Valladolid/Yucatán interior as a cavern-dive base with certified operators","si":"expedition","blurb":"Valladolid/Yucatán interior as a cavern-dive base with certified operators","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"dive-operator commission on application + DAN insurance affiliate"},{"name":"Ek Balam ruins (climbable acropolis) + Cenote X''Canche","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"~170 MXN cash + guided tour","source":"https://thehaphazardtraveler.com/ek-balam/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a Maya city 30 min N whose 32 m acropolis you can still climb, with rare intricate stucco façades; X''Canche swim 1.6 km away","si":"culture","blurb":"a Maya city 30 min N whose 32 m acropolis you can still climb, with rare intricate stucco façades; X''Canche swim 1.6 km away","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate (entry non-commissionable, cash-only)"},{"name":"Calzada de los Frailes + San Bernardino convent","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"free walk / guided colonial tour (convent evening sound-and-light)","source":"https://www.lugaresturisticosenmexico.com/en/valladolid-yucatan-pueblo-magico/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the pastel colonial spine of the Pueblo Mágico — a photogenic street of restored façades leading to the 16th-c. convent","si":"culture","blurb":"the pastel colonial spine of the Pueblo Mágico — a photogenic street of restored façades leading to the 16th-c. convent","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"walking-tour DMC + affiliate"},{"name":"Casa de los Venados (folk-art house-museum)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"donation-entry guided tour","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/HotelsNear-g499453-d1863475-Casa_de_los_Venados-Valladolid_Yucatan_Peninsula.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a private home + gallery holding 3,000+ pieces of Mexican folk & contemporary art — a singular cultural stop","si":"culture","blurb":"a private home + gallery holding 3,000+ pieces of Mexican folk & contemporary art — a singular cultural stop","when":"year-round","commission":"cultural-tour affiliate (donation non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Cochinita pibil in its heartland","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable":"food-tour + boutique stay","source":"https://cenotefinder.com/cenotes-in-mexico/valladolid-cenotes/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Valladolid is core Yucatecan-cuisine country — slow-roast cochinita pibil, longaniza, marquesitas; pair with a boutique-colonial stay","si":"culinary","blurb":"Valladolid is core Yucatecan-cuisine country — slow-roast cochinita pibil, longaniza, marquesitas; pair with a boutique-colonial stay","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"food-tour affiliate + host boutique booking"}],"faq":[{"q":"Which cenotes should I visit from Valladolid?","a":"Start with the three signatures. Zací is a swimmable sinkhole a 2-minute walk from the main square (free with a ~100 MXN restaurant meal) and the gentlest first swim; Suytun (~5 km east, ~250 MXN, open 9 AM–5 PM) delivers the iconic single light-beam onto its stone platform around 1–3 PM; and Oxman (150 MXN, or 350 with pool and lunch) is a deep, root-draped hacienda cenote with a rope swing. The Cuzamá/Homún horse-cart cenote country (~400 MXN/cart) adds a fourth day.","source":"dreambigtravelfarblog.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can you climb the ruins at Ek Balam?","a":"Yes — its 32 m acropolis is climbable, which sets Ek Balam apart from Chichén Itzá, where El Castillo has been off-limits since 2008. The site (~30 min north) has rare, intricate stucco façades and a swimmable cenote, X''Canche, 1.6 km away; entry is ~170 MXN, cash only, with no ATM on site.","source":"thehaphazardtraveler.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Valladolid a good base for the region?","a":"Yes — it is the mid-peninsula base the buses skip. Founded in 1543 and a Pueblo Mágico since 2012, it sits ~150 km from both Mérida and Cancún, ~40 min from Chichén Itzá, with a real layered bed market of boutique hotels, restored colonial casonas and haciendas — the slow-travel, colonial-romance alternative to the hot coast.","source":"thehaphazardtraveler.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What should I eat in Valladolid?","a":"This is core Yucatecan-cuisine country — slow-roast cochinita pibil, longaniza sausage and marquesita crêpes, amplified during the Hanal Pixán season. It pairs naturally with a boutique-colonial stay and an evening on the Calzada de los Frailes.","source":"cenotefinder.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at the cenotes?","a":"Heat and unguarded water. The cenotes and Ek Balam are best at the 9 AM opening before the heat builds; the cenotes are swim/snorkel with no lifeguards, so use provided life jackets (mandatory posture for non-swimmers and children), shower off sunscreen first, and mind slick stone platforms and rope swings. Drink bottled water only.","source":"dreambigtravelfarblog.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Valladolid Mexico 2026: Cenotes Suytun, Zací, Oxman & Ek Balam","meta_description":"Valladolid is a Yucatán Pueblo Mágico + cenote base — swim Zací, Suytun (light beam) and Oxman, climb Ek Balam, walk Calzada de los Frailes. Boutique stays, fees, cenote-dive safety.","slug":"valladolid-mexico","primary_keyword":"Valladolid Yucatán","long_tail":["cenotes Valladolid Suytun Zací Oxman","Cenote Suytun light beam best time","Ek Balam ruins from Valladolid","Valladolid Pueblo Mágico things to do","Cuzamá Homún horse cart cenotes","Valladolid boutique hotels"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["cenotes Valladolid","Cenote Suytun rayo de luz","Cenote Zací Valladolid","Cenote Oxman hacienda","ruinas Ek Balam Valladolid","Valladolid Pueblo Mágico qué hacer","cenotes Cuzamá Homún","Calzada de los Frailes","cochinita pibil Valladolid","hoteles boutique Valladolid"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"culinary","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Coqui Coqui Valladolid (Meson de Malleville)","tier":"premier-luxury BOUTIQUE (straight - design/intimacy/place, not 5-star resort)","why":"wellness/perfumery boutique brand in a colonial property; sell on soul not square footage","earning":"FIT/consortia (Fora/Virtuoso where property participates), commission on application","mor":"host MoR on stay + private tour; cenote/site fees non-commissionable","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/HotelsList-Valladolid-Boutique-Hotels-zfp12515607.html"},{"name":"Le Muuch Hotel Boutique","tier":"premier-luxury boutique (21 rooms, boho-chic design)","why":"intimate design boutique in the colonial core","earning":"FIT/consortia, commission on application","mor":"host MoR on stay","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/HotelsList-Valladolid-Boutique-Hotels-zfp12515607.html"},{"name":"Chable Yucatan (Merida circuit, ~2 hr W) - nearest TRUE ultra","tier":"ultra-luxury (Leading Hotels of the World)","why":"200-yr San Antonio hacienda, 750 acres, spa beside a sacred cenote, ~30 min from MID; base for private-guided Valladolid/cenote/Ek Balam/Chichen ultra day excursions","earning":"FIT/consortia (Virtuoso/Fora), commission on application","mor":"host MoR on stay + private tour","source":"https://www.lhw.com/hotel/Chable-Yucatan-Chochola-Merida-Mexico"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Valladolid, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.6896,"lng":-88.2011}}'::jsonb, 118),
  ('valle-de-guadalupe-mexico', '10S', 'Valle de Guadalupe, Mexico', 'Mexico', 'A Grenache poured at the vine that grew it', 'live', 'verified', 'restaurant', 'Baja California (Valle de Guadalupe & Ensenada)', '{"culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Mexico''s premier wine country — 100+ wineries along the Ruta del Vino, producing >90% of Mexican wine.","Baja Med farm-to-table anchors: Deckman''s en el Mogor (Michelin), Fauna, Corazón de Tierra, Finca Altozano.","Fiestas de la Vendimia (August) is the peak: 80+ wineries, 160+ labels, paella competition, pairing dinners.","Design wine-lodges: Banyan Tree Veya (30 villas, on-site Grenache winery), Encuentro/Endémico, Bruma.","Inside the Ensenada carve-out — Baja California is US L3 but the advisory names Ensenada NO-restriction."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","book_enabled":true,"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","state_dept_carveout":"Ensenada/Tijuana/Rosarito no-restriction","trauma":"Ensenada/Tijuana → San Diego US cross-border evacuation (US-standard trauma care) — a structural cross-border advantage","drink_driving":"always a designated driver / guided wine tour — never self-drive the tasting circuit","rural_road":"Hwy 3 + winery access roads are rural, partly unlit; daylight transfers only, no rural night driving","water":"bottled/filtered","air_access_verified":"Tijuana International (TIJ) via Cross Border Xpress (CBX) pedestrian bridge from San Diego (Otay Mesa), then ~1–1.5 hr drive on Hwy 3; or San Ysidro/Otay Mesa land crossing; Ensenada as coastal gateway. San Diego → Valle ~1h52m + border.","source":"https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/traveladvisories/traveladvisories/mexico-travel-advisory.html","accessed":"2026-07-07","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page